# 🗣️ COMMUNICATION PRACTICE

### Topic: **My Learning Strategy**

I have realized that effective learning is not about studying for long hours or memorizing large amounts of information. I learn better when I understand the reason behind a concept and connect it with something I already know. I usually break a difficult topic into smaller parts and study one part at a time. After learning it, I try to explain it in my own words and solve a few problems without looking at the solution. This helps me identify whether I actually understand the concept. I also believe revision is important because understanding something once does not guarantee that I will remember it later. Instead of repeatedly reading the same material, I prefer active recall and solving questions. My goal is to build knowledge that I can use in practical situations, technical interviews, projects, and examinations.

